<body>
  <div id="root"></div>
  <noscript>
    <h1>Fastino Labs</h1>
    <p>Fastino Labs builds open language and decision models for agentic AI, including GLiNER, GLiDE and the Fastino fine-tuning agent.</p>
    <p>Base URL: https://api.fastino.ai</p>
    <h2>Documentation</h2>
    <p>For the full machine-readable documentation, visit: <a href="https://docs.fastino.ai/llms.txt">https://docs.fastino.ai/llms.txt</a></p>
    <h2>Quick Start</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Get an API key from Settings → API Keys</li>
      <li>Upload or generate a dataset (JSON, JSONL, or CSV)</li>
      <li>Start a training job with POST /v1/training/jobs</li>
      <li>Evaluate with project-scoped Evaluation Suites</li>
      <li>Run inference with POST /v1/chat/completions, or get a GLiDE decision with POST /v1/systemone</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>API Formats</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>GLiDE decisions: POST /v1/systemone with model fastino/GLiDE</li>
      <li>OpenAI-compatible: POST /v1/chat/completions (set base_url to https://api.fastino.ai/v1)</li>
      <li>Anthropic-compatible: POST /v1/messages (set base_url to https://api.fastino.ai)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Auth: Include your API key in the X-API-Key header. Keys start with fast_sk_ (pio_sk_ keys are retired).</p>
    <p>Full documentation: <a href="https://docs.fastino.ai/llms.txt">https://docs.fastino.ai/llms.txt</a></p>
  </noscript>
</body>

</html>
